                <airSeal>Air sealing beyond the % mentioned above will result in more significant savings. This could be difficult to achieve unless performed during other renovation upgrades (walls, ceiling). </airSeal>
                <ceilings>Insulating the attic is a simple and affordable way to save energy. Blown cellulose or fibreglass are the most common methods. </ceilings>
                <HeatingSystem>As this house uses electric baseboard heat I highly recommend installing a Cold Climate Heat Pump. They are affordable to install, as well as eligible for Good Energy rebates. Heat pumps will operate at 200% efficiency on average over traditional electric heat.  I can provide more information on brands and models for our climate if requested. 



